# SABOTAGE: P5 (ADR-048 §8, operator ruling D-04) — the kill-switch re-check at the LEVEL 2
# RETRY boundary is REMOVED from `Samen.AI.Agent.complete_with_recovery/10`. This is the
# sabotage-244 shape ONE LEVEL DOWN: 244 removes the re-check at the TURN boundary in
# `loop/5`, so an operator kill landing between turn N and turn N+1 is silently ignored;
# THIS removes it at the RETRY boundary, so a kill landing DURING the overflowing attempt
# is silently ignored and Level 2 derives a fold and spends a SECOND provider call after
# someone has already hit the emergency stop. The kill-switch is the emergency stop: a
# compaction retry must not proceed after it is hit.
#
# Flips the named P5 red. Everything else stays GREEN, which is what makes the red mean
# what it says: the P5 POSITIVE CONTROL (the byte-identical script WITHOUT the kill, in
# which the retry DOES happen) still passes, and 244's own turn-boundary red
# (`a kill flipped DURING turn 2 stops turn 3`) and its positive control still pass — so
# the red fails because the RETRY-boundary re-check is gone, not because Level 2, the
# turn boundary, or the switch itself broke. C2's Level 2 bound is untouched: the
# `attempt <= @max_context_retries and context_overflow?(result)` clause and its
# `derive_fold/8` + recursive call are left exactly as they are.
#
# Deletes ONE CONTIGUOUS `cond` clause and its comment, replacing it with a `# SABOTAGE`
# comment, so the file still compiles under `--warnings-as-errors` (an `if false do`
# shape would trip Elixir's always-same-result warning). Touches agent.ex ALONE.
#
# Re-anchored at HEAD `68eb340` (operator ruling D-14) after D-13's `over_budget/2` arm
# shifted this clause's position; D-13's arm is deliberately preserved as unmodified
# trailing context here, not deleted.
# Re-anchored again for issue #11 (bill the failed attempt): the D-17 billing step now
# sits between `retries = attempt - 1` and this `cond`, and the §6 comment above it was
# rewritten, so the old context no longer matched. Same deletion, same semantics.
# Re-anchored a third time for the #11 follow-up: `bill_failed_attempt` now returns the
# turn row too, so the line above this `cond` changed. Same deletion, same semantics.
